
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
C,A,B are collinear [00]
CB = CA [01]
CD = CB [02]
DE ⟂ AB [03]
DF ⟂ CD [04]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
G : Points
F,G,D are collinear [05]

 * Proof steps:
001. CB = CA [01] & CD = CB [02] ⇒  C is the circumcenter of \Delta DAB [06]
002. C is the circumcenter of \Delta DAB [06] & C,A,B are collinear [00] ⇒  AD ⟂ BD [07]
003. C,A,B are collinear [00] & DE ⟂ AB [03] & AD ⟂ BD [07] ⇒  ∠ADB = ∠(ED-CA) [08]
004. C is the circumcenter of \Delta DAB [06] & DF ⟂ CD [04] ⇒  ∠FDB = ∠DAB [09]
005. C,A,B are collinear [00] & F,G,D are collinear [05] & ∠DAB = ∠FDB [09] ⇒  ∠DAC = ∠(FG-BD) [10]
006. ∠ADB = ∠(ED-CA) [08] & ∠DAC = ∠(FG-BD) [10] ⇒  ∠(AD-FG) = ∠EDA [11]
007. ∠(AD-FG) = ∠EDA [11] & F,G,D are collinear [05] ⇒  ∠ADF = ∠EDA
==========================
